  "final_message": "Wait for test execution to complete.\nI am checking the repository commit history to understand the design rules and conventions.\nWait for branch check.\nWait for git log.\nWait for npm run arch to finish.\nI am waiting for the dependency cruiser check to finish.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI cannot directly remove `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model due to architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L28):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**:\n   [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is an external integration event consumed across repository boundaries by `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. Directly removing the `channel` field is a breaking schema change that violates ARCH-4.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**:\n   Because [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) populates `channel` from [`Order.channel`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L23), removing it from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) would prevent emitting the required field to existing consumers.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\nTo remove this field safely in accordance with ARCH-4:\n- Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n- Coordinate the deprecation timeline with the `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` teams.\n- Once downstream consumers have been updated and deployed, plan a schema migration to remove `channel`.\n",
